1
00:00:00,508 --> 00:00:03,568
- Then what's yourjob?
- Letting him make me happy.

2
00:00:05,613 --> 00:00:08,813
(Bernadette:)I just think, in relationships,
you get back what you put in.

3
00:00:09,050 --> 00:00:10,380
(Amy:)That's not always true.

4
00:00:10,585 --> 00:00:13,075
(Amy:)Last night I gave Sheldon
my best come-hither look...

5
00:00:13,287 --> 00:00:17,557
(Amy:)...and he responded by explaining
how wheat came to be cultivated.

6
00:00:18,659 --> 00:00:21,029
(Penny:)I guess I could probably try a little harder.

7
00:00:21,429 --> 00:00:23,829
(Bernadette:)You could start
by taking an interest in his work.

8
00:00:24,065 --> 00:00:26,035
(Penny:)- That's kind of a problem.
- Why?

9
00:00:26,234 --> 00:00:28,464
(Penny:)Not really clear on what he does.

10
00:00:29,103 --> 00:00:30,933
(Bernadette:)He's an experimental physicist.

11
00:00:31,138 --> 00:00:33,668
(Penny:)Yeah, I'm not really clear
on what that means.

12
00:00:34,842 --> 00:00:39,282
(Amy:)He takes hypotheses and designs protocols
to determine their accuracy.

13
00:00:39,480 --> 00:00:41,970
(Penny:)Yeah, you're really just making it worse.

14
00:00:44,185 --> 00:00:46,175
(Sheldon:)What kind of tea would you like?

15
00:00:46,420 --> 00:00:50,860
I think I'm going to try
green tea mixed with lemon zinger.

16
00:00:51,092 --> 00:00:53,852
(Sheldon:)Two tea bags in one cup?

17
00:00:54,495 --> 00:01:00,025
(Sheldon:)You're not at a rave.

